\begin{equation}
\hat{s} = W_2 \, \mathrm{ReLU}(W_1 \, f_t + b_1) + b_2,
\end{equation}
where $W_1 \in \mathbb{R}^{256 \times 1024}$, $W_2 \in \mathbb{R}^{1 \times 256}$, and $\hat{s} \in \mathbb{R}^{B \times H}$ gives the predicted minimum signed distance for each timestep in the action chunk. The head contains approximately 263K parameters, which is negligible compared to the 300M-parameter action expert.

\paragraph{Ground-truth SDF computation.} Per-timestep signed distances are precomputed offline using MuJoCo's \texttt{mj\_geomDistance}, measuring minimum distance between end-effector geometries and scene obstacles (excluding grasped objects). Labels are stored as compressed arrays and aligned to action chunks at training time. Implementation details are in Appendix~\ref{app:sdf_labels}.
